# Files that stay on your Mac and never go up to GitHub.

# The raw Apple Health export. It's 15 MB, and git keeps a complete copy of
# every version forever — twenty updates would bloat the repository to a few
# hundred megabytes for no benefit. The app doesn't read this file anyway; it
# reads health.json, which build.py generates from it.
#
# Keep the CSV here as your archive. Just don't publish it.
Healthstats.csv
*.csv

# Your encryption passphrase, if you chose to save it rather than type it on
# every update. This must NEVER reach GitHub — it's the one thing standing
# between a passer-by and your health data.
.passphrase

# macOS clutter
.DS_Store
